From 6df0bd65cce6511622a5f2d6b80a6a64d66618de Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 02:01:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] windowing/gbm: the player information is published while
 Check this setup plays its clips

"Check this setup" of the LibreELEC settings plays short test clips of
LibreELEC Hades and says in a sentence what went out and how: the
display mode, the HDR signal that the driver holds, whether Dolby Vision
went out natively and why not, what the sound output opened (a bitstream
and its format, or PCM in so many channels), the pictures dropped, and
the sentence of the overview page of the player information
(hades.sum.*). Kodi decides all of that already, for that page; but the
values of the page (hades.out.*, hades.audio.*, hades.video.*,
hades.play.*, hades.sum.*) are published only while the page is shown,
and opening it over a test picture would draw over the picture that the
check asks the user to look at.

The check now sets the property hades.check.running of the Home window
to 1 while its clips play. PublishPlayerInfo() publishes the values then
as it does for the page, at most twice a second, and takes them all
away again when the property goes, as when the page closes. The GPU is
not read for the check (no sampler thread) and nothing is lit: those
are for the page only (PublishingFor()). The property is looked at
twice a second at most (CPolledFlag), so a frame that no one reads the
values for costs a clock reading and a comparison; nothing else runs
unless the check is running.

utils/PlayerInfoPublishing.h holds the rule and the polled flag, with
their host test (TestPlayerInfoPublishing).
